ready to explore your options, visit our [pricing page](https://emmystack01.com/pricing) to learn\
more about Emmy STACK01's offerings.

**9. What Should Your First Business Website Include?**

If you've\
decided that your business is ready for a website, you don't need to\
overcomplicate the process.

Start\
with the essentials.

**A clear homepage**

Your\
homepage should quickly communicate what your business does, who it serves, and\
how visitors can get started.

A\
first-time visitor shouldn't have to search through several pages to understand\
what you're offering.

**An about page**

Introduce\
your business, explain what you do, and help visitors understand what makes\
your approach or offering different.

Keep the\
focus on information that matters to your potential customers.

**A services or products page**

Clearly\
explain what you offer.

Include\
relevant descriptions, images, pricing where appropriate, and any details\
customers need to make informed decisions.

**A portfolio or testimonials section**

If your\
business has completed projects or received customer feedback, use genuine\
examples to demonstrate your experience.

If you're\
just starting, you can focus on explaining your process, showcasing relevant\
sample work, or presenting your initial offerings honestly.

**Clear contact information**

Make it\
easy for customers to reach you.

Depending\
on your business, this could include a phone number, email address, WhatsApp\
link, physical address, enquiry form, or booking link.

**A mobile-friendly design**

Many\
customers will visit your website using their phones.

Your\
pages should load reasonably quickly, your text should be easy to read, and\
your buttons should be easy to use on smaller screens.

**Basic SEO and technical setup**

Your\
website should have clear page titles, descriptive content, a sensible page\
structure, and the technical foundations needed for search engines to discover\
and understand it.

Depending\
on your business, you may also benefit from a Google Business Profile,\
especially if you serve customers in a specific location.

You can\
add more features as your business grows.

The best\
starting point is a website that serves your customers well and supports your\
most important business goals.

